# @DISTRO_NAME@ power defaults (docs/ENTERPRISE.md, ADR-0017). Users change them in Fab Settings > Power Management; the
# per-user ~/.config/powerdevilrc overrides this file. Key names verified in the image's libpowerdevilcore.so.6.6.6
# (UTF-16 literals: LidAction, AutoSuspendAction, AutoSuspendIdleTimeoutSec, TurnOffDisplayIdleTimeoutSec, profile groups
# AC / Battery / LowBattery, section SuspendAndShutdown). LidAction=1 = sleep when the lid is closed (PowerDevil's
# PowerButtonAction::SuspendSession), the upstream default restated so it is asserted; on wake the screen is locked by
# kscreenlocker's LockOnResume=true (/etc/xdg/kscreenlockerrc [Daemon]), which is how "lock on lid close" is realised.
[AC][SuspendAndShutdown]
LidAction=1

[Battery][SuspendAndShutdown]
LidAction=1

[LowBattery][SuspendAndShutdown]
LidAction=1
